From 058270ad0de89f9b46ef8ad571a89c8dd11bd6bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: toxic <toxic@local>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 12:40:53 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] fix(providers): per-provider unbounded retry-after cap
 for opencode-zen/go
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

OpenCode Go and Zen (free tier) return 429 `retry-after-ms=21431000` on
daily-quota exhaustion. Today that hint exceeds both the 60s transport
cap (`fetchWithRetry.maxDelayMs`) and the 5min `retry.maxDelayMs`
fail-fast in TurnRecovery, surfacing the long wait as a hard error.

Plumb a per-provider retry config end-to-end:

- `ProviderDefinition.retry: { maxRetryDelayMs?, unboundedRetryAfter? }`.
- Opencode Go and Zen opt into `unboundedRetryAfter: true`.
- `resolveProviderMaxRetryDelayMs` (caller > unbounded > provider default
  > undefined) is consulted in `mapOptionsForApi` and threaded into
  `OpenAIStreamRequestInit` / `postOpenAIStream` / `fetchWithRetry`.
- `TurnRecovery` skips the `exceeds retry.maxDelayMs` fail-fast when
  `message.provider` is registered as unbounded.
- `providers.unboundedRetryAfter` (string array, default
  ["opencode-go", "opencode-zen"]) overrides `retry.maxDelayMs`
  in the settings-aware stream fn; user-configurable.

Tests:
- `packages/ai/test/retry-config.test.ts` — registry + resolver contract.
- `packages/ai/test/openai-http-retry-cap.test.ts` — `postOpenAIStream`
  forwards `maxRetryDelayMs` to `fetchWithRetry.maxDelayMs`.
